IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-art11-application`
IMPORT `g4-art11-decision`
IMPORT `g4-art12-name`
IMPORT `g4-tests-fixtures`

-- g4-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT TO FAIL, and whose failures are counted (14; check.sh lists the count).
-- Each of the first thirteen states, under the reading the encoding takes, the answer that a DIFFERENT reading of the same fork gives: the answer a reader who took the other reading would expect.
-- It fails exactly because the readings differ on the discriminating case of the fork (g4-tests-forks.l4 asserts the right answers on each reading). The fourteenth misuses `#ASSERT REFUSED` on an expression that answers.
-- Together they show that the harness can fail, and that each fork's discriminating case discriminates: if the encoding ever took the other reading, the corresponding assertion would turn green and the forks module would turn red.

§ `Assertions meant to fail`

-- F4.1: on the default reading the day of the application is outside the twelve months (reading B puts it inside). EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2026 3 15)

-- F4.1: on the default reading 14 March 2025 is outside the twelve months (reading C puts it inside). EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2025 3 14)

-- F4.2: on the default reading the date of the application is the day it is lodged (reading B: the day it is complete), so the payment of 10 March 2026 is outside the window. EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026`

-- F4.3: with the copy of the constitution missing and the six matters found, reading B says the Commissioner must refuse; the default reading says no duty arises. EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the base case` `but with the application as` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)) EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

-- F4.4: with a fitness issue undetermined, reading B says the Commissioner must register; the default reading says not yet. EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`

-- F4.5: a name the same as that of a deregistered charity is, on the default reading, not undesirable (reading B says it is). EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of a charity that has been deregistered`))

-- F4.6: a year before 29 February 2028 is, on the default reading, 28 February 2027 (reading B: 1 March 2027). EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` `the default reading` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1

-- F4.7: a name the same as another charity's alternative registered name is, on the default reading, undesirable (reading B compares only the registered name). EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `an alternative registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))

-- F4.8: on the default reading an unrelated previous registered name is not a name the charity may use (reading B says it is). EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name`

-- F4.9: with 30 days from 1 March 2026, a decision on 31 March 2026 is in time on the default reading (reading B: late). Asserted late. EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 3 31)

-- F4.10: on the default reading the caller's determination decides, whatever the dates; asserted that 59 days is not within 30. EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `the default reading` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST 30)

-- F4.11: a payment to someone who became a governor only after being paid is not reached on the default reading (reading B reaches it). Asserted reached. EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `the default reading` `the base application` `payment of 700 to Dina on 1 December 2025, who became a governor later`

-- F4.12: a ground of discretionary refusal whose circumstances are present but which should not be applied does not defeat matter (f) on the default reading (reading B says it does). Asserted that it does. EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `the default reading` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground whose circumstances are present as` TRUE)

-- A refusal asserted of an expression that answers: `#ASSERT REFUSED` fails with "expected a refusal, but the expression produced a value". EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11 the date of the application` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete`
